  "verbalization": "Ethambutol's potential repurposing for Pulmonary Tuberculosis is supported by its off-label use in Mycobacterial Infectious Disease, which is a key pathway in the evidence. This off-label use links Ethambutol to Cycloserine and Ethionamide, both of which have indications for Pulmonary Tuberculosis. The shared mechanism of action in Mycobacterial Infectious Disease suggests that Ethambutol may exert some therapeutic effect in this context, even if it is not approved for direct use in Pulmonary Tuberculosis. The evidence highlights a potential role of Ethambutol in treating Mycobacterial Infections, possibly through indirect pathways involving other antimicrobial agents. The integration of these off-label uses underscores the importance of considering broader pharmacological relationships in drug repurposing, particularly when traditional indications are not sufficient.",
